  "post_text": "US hiring is showing no signs of a recovery.\n\nNew job postings on Indeed fell -4.8% YoY in the week ending October 16th.\n\nSince April 2022, new job postings have now declined -46.7%.\n\nAs a result, the number of new available vacancies in the US is -0.8% below pre-pandemic levels recorded in February 2020.\n\nOver the last several months, the pace of decline has slowed, but there have been no signs of a rebound in hiring either.\n\nThis suggests a lack of a significant recovery in official BLS job openings data, which lags job postings data by a few weeks.\n\nThe US labor market remains weak beneath the surface.",
